arry on average about (n−1)/2 days of demand each evening.\n- **Every 4 days** (3, 5, 6): about 1.5 days of stock. That costs roughly 300 more in storage than ordering every 3 days and saves only one or two fees. Item 1 also has only one day to sell its leftovers before they expire.\n- **Every 3 days** (0, 2, 4): 9 orders, about 1 day of stock.\n- **Every 2 days** (Candidate 1): 12 orders, which is 3 more fees (+147). But it carries only about 0.5 day of stock, which saves roughly 11 per day, or about 275 over the period. That's a net gain of about 130 over Candidate 0. Smaller deliveries also stay well below the 172-unit storage limit.\n- **Every day** (Candidate 7): 26 orders, about 690 more in fees than Candidate 1, while saving only about another 275 in storage. Clearly worse.\n\n**Why Candidate 1 wins.** It orders about ×1.08 of forecast for both items, which is slightly above average demand. Each short cycle is backed by the previous delivery's leftovers, so it holds up well when actual demand differs from the forecast. Candidate 0 (every 3 days, ×1.1 for item 0 and ×1.05 for item 1) comes second, behind by about the storage cost difference."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3838, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3838}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:33:02.014Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQYAUy3tCD41KshPXxr1"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01RhZSdvYs7TNaUTjGvipbf2", "nam