does worse than candidate 0.\n- **Candidate 4** over-orders by about 76 more units of product 0 than candidate 0, plus extra product 1. The surplus means unsold stock at the end (8 per unit), storage fees and expired product 1. It also nearly overflows the 172-unit warehouse around day 20.\n- **Candidate 3** orders too little of product 0 (521).\n- **Candidates 5 and 6** carry larger stocks because of the 4-day cycle. That costs about 240 more in storage than a 3-day cycle, which outweighs saving one order fee. They also overflow the warehouse on days 9, 13, 21 and especially 25 (candidate 5 loses about 18 units of product 1 that day).\n- **Candidate 7** saves only about 280 in storage compared with candidate 1 but pays 637 more in order fees. That puts it roughly 350 behind.\n\n**Candidate 1 vs candidate 0.** Ordering every 2 days instead of every 3 halves the average evening stock. That saves about 11.5 × 0.3 × 25 ≈ 86 in storage for product 0 and about 11 × 0.7 × 25 ≈ 193 for product 1, roughly 279 in total. The four extra orders cost 196, so candidate 1 comes out ahead by about 80. It also has no warehouse-capacity problems. Its slightly larger product 1 buffer partly makes up for having more points where a shortage can occur. With random demand, a difference of about 80 can easily flip, hence the probability of about 0.5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3887, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3887}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:34:07.457Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQY8s4GwN2uax16iPde3"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "paren